  "title": "infiniband/smbdirect: fix dissecting the first smbdirect negotiate request",
  "description": "Here's a sample capture\nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark-web/-/issues/62\nhttps://gitlab.com/-/project/22852016/uploads/538c095d29f38f95b5231fd7b9e05bdf/rdma2-rxe-r6.18-tmp-10.pcap.gz\nThis is a Windows server 2025 as server with an Intel-E810-CQDA2 card in\nroce v2 mode (10.123.102.5) and smbclient kernel smbdirect using\nsoftware roce rdma_rxe (10.123.102.4) This uses smb signing so there's\nno rdma offload for the write.\n\nThis fixes dissecting of frame 6, while reassembling still works\nat the infiniband layer, e.g. frames 50 + 51, as well\nas the smbdirect layer, see how frame 51 is part of frame 2388.\n\nSigned-off-by: Stefan Metzmacher <metze@samba.org>",
